{
 "id": "2023-li-demographic",
 "name": "Demographic Differences in Liking Subway Entrance Pavilions (9 Renderings, 1–5)",
 "description": "Faithful replication of the online survey in Li, Han, Shen, Wang, Gu, Yang & Zhang (2023), \"A Demographic Characteristics-Based Study on the Visual Impact Assessment of the External Form of Entrance Pavilions to the Underground Stations of China's Subway\", Applied Sciences 13(6):4030. Participants see the paper's nine renderings (A–I) of real subway entrance pavilions in Changsha, Taiyuan, Tianjin, Shanghai, Chengdu, Xi'an, Beijing, Xiamen and Nanning (modelled by the authors in SketchUp and rendered with V-Ray at 167 cm eye height under a clear sky) in random order and score each from 1 (strongly dislike) to 5 (strongly like); scores can be revised before submitting. Gender, age group (18–34, 35–59, 60+), education level (higher education or not) and design experience follow, the four demographic variables the paper compares. The paper (N = 320) found the highest mean for H (4.15) and the lowest for G (2.07), and related scores to exterior contour, façade permeability, cultural characteristics, materials and number of colours. Renderings are cropped from the paper's Figure 4 (CC BY 4.0); credit to the authors, and the template will be removed if the authors object. Differences from the original study: (1) the paper collected demographics in a separate first questionnaire and then sent the rating questionnaire to a quota sample; here both are in one survey, demographics at the end; (2) a consent page is added; (3) the renderings are cropped from the published figure, without its captions and A–I letters, and shown at web resolution.",
